<title>FRANCE: France aims to save 1.01 bln via generic medicines.</title>
<headline>France aims to save 1.01 bln via generic medicines.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French government said on Monday it hoped to save 1.01 billion francs next year by encouraging the use of generic medicines.</p>
<p>It said in a statement a decree defining the use of generic medicines would be published in mid-October.</p>
<p>The government is seeking to reduce the welfare deficit to 29.7 billion francs next year from a forecast 51.6 billion francs this year through cost curbs and higher taxes.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
